# Extract's own Pass A fixture (U6a.2-3), not a ladder rung: the declaration hazards the ladder does not
# hold yet. Written by hand from ws/ in the ladder's format (fixtures/ladder/README.md) and checked by
# packages/extract/src/ladder.test.ts. It lists Pass A's facts only: decorator CALLs (decision 107's
# other half) and every other call are Pass B (U6a.2-4), and SOURCE_FILE is the engine's (C-EXTRACT Q8).
#
# decl.py: a module MEMBER and its redefinition, a decorated function (its range starts at the
# decorator), splat and typed parameters, a nested def that is not descended (decision 92), an async
# def with separators, a decorated class with a tuple assignment (no MEMBER), a constructor, a
# property's getter and setter (one name twice: the second takes ordinal 1 and DEFINES the same
# SYMBOL), a nested class, and a private class.
# broken.py: ERROR regions directly under the module and under a class body (decision 95).

